te","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNote","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidental":{"title":"MXLAccidental","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidental"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The accidental type represents actual notated accidentals. Editorial and cautionary indications are indicated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by attributes. Values for these attributes are “no” if not present. Specific graphic display such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parentheses, brackets, and size are controlled by the level-display attribute group."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidental"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidental","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidental"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/accidental":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/accidental","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"accidental"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"type